# AGENTS.local.md

Personal agent context. Copy this file to `AGENTS.local.md` at the repo root and
fill it in. `AGENTS.local.md` is gitignored, so it can hold details that must
not be shared: addresses, user names, local paths, your own way of working.

- Shared rules belong in `AGENTS.md` or a component's `AGENTS.md`, not here. If
  you learn something the whole team needs, move it there in a pull request.
- Never put passwords, API keys or tokens in this file either. Keep them in your
  shell environment or in the gitignored `node/node.conf` (mode 600).
- Claude Code reads `CLAUDE.md` files, not `AGENTS.md`. To load both files,
  create a gitignored `CLAUDE.local.md` at the repo root containing:

  ```
  @AGENTS.md
  @AGENTS.local.md
  ```

  Other tools: see `docs/02_Engineering/03_Agent_Context.md`.

---

## How I want agents to work

Delete the lines that don't apply, and add your own.

- Ask me when anything is unclear. Don't make design decisions on your own.
  For a real choice, give me the options and a recommendation.
- Say whether you can reach the hardware. If you can't, give me short, exact
  commands to run, say which terminal and which physical pin, and say what
  output to expect.
- Before any loopback test, have me confirm the wiring with `pinctrl`.
- Before I connect anything external, remind me of the 74LVC245 buffer, the
  series resistors and the shared ground. Never let me connect pin 1 (3.3 V) or
  pins 2 and 4 (5 V) to a GPIO.
- Commit message trailer my tool should add: `<trailer or none>`.

## My environment

- Operating system: `<OS and version>`
- How I build and test: `<dev container | setup_host.sh | other>`
- Repo location: `<path on this machine>` (never copy this into shared files)
- Known limits of this machine: `<for example low disk space, no Docker>`
- Where my credentials come from: `<for example exported in my shell>`

## My Pi

- Model and RAM: `<Raspberry Pi 5, 8 GB>`
- OS and kernel: `<Raspberry Pi OS Bookworm, uname -r output>`
- Address: `<hostname or IP>` (this is what `<pi-host>` means in the docs)
- ssh user: `<user>`
- Install folder: `<path>` (this is what `<install_dir>` means in the docs)
- `/dev/pio0` permissions and my `gpio` group membership: `<ls -l /dev/pio0>`
- RP1 firmware and op count, if known: `<value>`
- UART on GPIO 14 enabled: `<yes or no>`
- What is wired right now: `<for example loopback jumper pin 38 to pin 3>`

## Open items

- `<things I am in the middle of, with the next command to run>`
